WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.610 --> 00:00:07.880
On this day exactly 99 years ago the WW1 treaty
dealing with the Hungarian half of the Austro-Hungarian

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.740
Empire, the Treaty of Trianon, came into effect.

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.940
This video is sponsored by World of Tanks.

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:17.800
Which is giving new players some extra benefits
to play around with but more on that later.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.930
Before watching this video I suggest you watch
my previous two videos on the break up of

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:24.540
Austria-Hungary and the Treaty of Saint Germain.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:28.170
Also before we talk about the main events
I want to have a few quick side notes about

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.870
some extra things that happened during this
time but don’t connect well to the main

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:33.160
story of the video.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.530
So the area in the East Carpathian mountains
and a bit south of it mostly populated by

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.350
Slavic speaking Rusyn people is today known
as Ruthenia.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:45.630
During the breakup of the Austro-Hungarian
empire Rusyns didn’t just stand idle by

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.650
and in fact they formed several councils to
try to figure out what should be the future

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.650
for Ruthenia.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:51.650
Of these councils there were 4 main ones each
with a different idea of what they wanted.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:54.670
First was the council in Presov which was
at the beginning divided among people wanting

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:59.490
to unite with Czechoslovakia or with Russia,
but at the time they were unaware of the whole

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:03.829
scope of the actual civil war happening in
Russia and when they became aware of it the

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:06.890
council fully decided to unite with Czechoslovakia.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.810
The second council was in Uzhorod this council
decided on trying to push for self autonomy

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.630
within the new state of Hungary.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:18.780
The last two councils were in Máramaros Sighet
and Yasinya, both of these councils initially

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.970
wanted to unite with Ukraine but when it became
clear that wouldn’t be possible due to the

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:27.440
Ukranian defeat by the Bolsheviks and the
Poles, the Máramaros Sighet council agreed

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.740
to uniting with Czechoslovakia all while the
Yasinya council declared independence proclaiming

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.300
the Hutsul Republic.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.590
As post war negotiations dragged on and it
started to become clear that Karolyi’s government

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:43.600
in Hungary wasn’t going to give a lot of
autonomy to Ruthenia, the council in Uzhorod

00:01:43.600 --> 00:01:46.150
also agreed on a unification with Czechoslovakia.

00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:50.740
So the last hold out at this point was the
Hutsul Republic which over all governed only

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:56.270
around 20 thousand people and existed only
thanks to the help of troops from the WUPR.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:02:03.200
So when the WUPR ended in 1919 they also had
no choice but to accept unification with Czechoslovakia.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:07.720
The Presov council during these negotiations
also unified with the Lemko Rusyn council

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:12.970
which declared independence in southern Poland
and hoped for unification with Czechoslovakia.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.090
Their argument being that rather than remaining
in Poland they wanted to join the country

00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:21.099
which many of their brothers in Ruthenia have
decided to join as well.

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:25.511
However, the Lemko Rusyn Republic got conquered
by the Poles and Czechoslovakia didn’t want

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:31.290
to sture up anymore problems with Poland after
the whole war over Tesin, so the Lemko Rusyn

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:35.180
republic wasn’t allowed to join Czechoslovakia
along with its brothers in Ruthenia.

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:41.200
In the end outside of a few disgruntled Rusyns
most of Ruthenia joined Czechoslovakia willingly

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:46.099
hoping to benefit from the strong post war
economy of Czechoslovakia and gain more autonomy

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:48.240
than it had under the Hungarians.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.950
Whether this will happen is a story for another
time.

00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:53.360
We also have to talk about southern Hungary.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:57.860
Here not as much happened as elsewhere within
the crumbling Empire mostly because actual

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:02.700
allied troops were stationed in Serbia since
that’s where the front line ended in 1918.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:07.500
Plus Hungary already going into the Belgrade
negotiations gave up any idea of trying to

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:12.420
retain control over Croatia and parts of Slovenia
so there was no major fighting there.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.870
But all this is not to say that nothing happened.

00:03:14.870 --> 00:03:19.010
For one Yugoslav troops overstepped their
demarcation lines occupying border towns like

00:03:19.010 --> 00:03:22.840
Pecs that were supposed to remain demilitarized
by both sides.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.530
Then there was the Banat Republic that was
declared in the confusion of the break up

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:31.260
of Austria-Hungary, however, this republic
even though officially ending on February

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:36.540
20th 1919 didn’t really have much power
since the allied occupation of the area in

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.710
November 1918.

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:43.740
There was also a Serbian-Hungarian Baranya-Baja
Republic centered around Pecs that was established

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:49.860
14 of August 1921 when Yugoslav troops withdrew
from the area but it only lasted for 6 days

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.190
before Horthy came in and took control.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.150
Those were my extra side notes now back to
Hungary.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:01.360
By January 1919 when the Paris Peace conference
started every single Hungarian was furious

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:05.980
because on top of having no coal for the winter
as Czechoslovakia blocked coal shipments to

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:11.510
Hungary, there were also food shortages, uncontrollable
inflation, shrinking economy, etc.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:16.310
By some accounts people said that the year
after the war was worse than the years during

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:17.609
the actual war.

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:22.590
But despite all of this nothing made the Hungarians
more furious than the high loss of land they

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:25.610
have suffered under the allied occupation
demands.

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:30.369
This was then further exacerbated by the fact
that in the following months of early 1919

00:04:30.369 --> 00:04:35.289
the Romanian and Czechoslovak demarcation
lines continued to be pushed further and further

00:04:35.289 --> 00:04:39.839
into Hungary, these demarcation changes were
sometimes purely as a further land grab by

00:04:39.839 --> 00:04:44.509
the neighboring nations or sometimes because
the French or British allied commanders felt

00:04:44.509 --> 00:04:49.139
a strategically important railroad track or
a vallie up ahead was a better defendable

00:04:49.139 --> 00:04:50.139
position.

00:04:50.139 --> 00:04:54.870
Hungary again had no choice but to concede
to these new lines being established.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.809
With all this happening almost every Hungarian
started blaming Károlyi and his government

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:01.669
for the major loss of land.

00:05:01.669 --> 00:05:06.349
In fact Károlyi is still blamed by Hungarians
today for this entire situation, pointing

00:05:06.349 --> 00:05:10.600
to his pacifist attitude, premature demilitarization
and the fact that he sought out a seperate

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:14.119
armistice agreement in Belgrade, as the major
points of his failure.

00:05:14.119 --> 00:05:19.509
However that is completely unfair, the allies
already promised land to the neighboring nations

00:05:19.509 --> 00:05:24.059
of Hungary during the war, so no matter if
the Belgrade armistice happened or not the

00:05:24.059 --> 00:05:29.330
partition of Hungary would have happened either
way most likely exactly the same way it did.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.839
Plus Hungary lost the war, they were in no
position to resist any allied demands/occupation,

00:05:33.839 --> 00:05:39.590
if Károlyi wouldn’t have disbanded the
army early on as he did and would have tried

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:44.869
to confront the allied demands with it, it
would only lead to further unnecessary Hungarian

00:05:44.869 --> 00:05:48.490
deaths with the outcome being exactly the
same maybe even worse.

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:49.490
Therefore Károlyi shouldn’t be blamed for
Hungary's situation after the Great War, no

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:53.259
matter who was in charge of Hungary during
that time the outcome would have been the

00:05:53.259 --> 00:05:56.590
same because the main factors wouldn’t have
changed.

00:05:56.590 --> 00:06:00.990
Hungary lost the war, allies promised land
to the neighboring nations and minorities

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:06.389
across the country rose up establishing independent
administrations, there’s no changing that.

00:06:06.389 --> 00:06:12.889
However such thinking was outright non existent
among the hungairan people in 1919, the thinking

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:18.539
that did prevail was that Hungary lost 2/3rds
of its land and something had to be done about

00:06:18.539 --> 00:06:19.539
it.

00:06:19.539 --> 00:06:23.949
So when Károlyi’s government received yet
another letter from Paris that increased the

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:28.409
Romanian demarcation line roughly to the area
of where today’s borders between Hungary

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:33.089
and Romania are, he along with his government
refused to accept it because they couldn’t

00:06:33.089 --> 00:06:36.800
accept it without another major revolution
happening in Hungary.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:42.669
So they instead resigned in late March creating
a power vacuum, a power vacuum which a man

00:06:42.669 --> 00:06:47.949
sent by Lenin, Bela Kun along with his communist
supporters quickly took advantage of in a

00:06:47.949 --> 00:06:52.319
pretty much bloodless coup, forming the Hungarian
Soviet Republic.

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:56.479
Also at this point due to the government change
in Hungary the Paris peace negotiations dealing

00:06:56.479 --> 00:06:59.659
with Hungary were put on hold.

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:06.270
The new Hungarian Soviet Republic was universally
welcomed by all Hungarians, not just the proletariat,

00:07:06.270 --> 00:07:10.429
this was because the main stated goal of the
communists was to regain control over all

00:07:10.429 --> 00:07:15.530
of the lost land, a sentiment which was shared
by all Hungairan people regardless of their

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.530
political views.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:22.110
The Communists quickly started rearming and
planning to first reconquer Transilvania before

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:23.759
turning to Slovakia.

00:07:23.759 --> 00:07:27.629
Also during this time even though the coup
was bloodless sadly the same cannot be said

00:07:27.629 --> 00:07:33.509
about the regime itself which endorsed many
killings of people who were deemed anti-communist,

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:37.300
they also supported attacks on minorities
still living within Hungary.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:40.710
These killings became to be known as the Red
Terror in Hungary.

00:07:40.710 --> 00:07:44.650
While this was happening Romania asked the
allies for a permission to depose the new

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:49.009
communist government, but to the dismay of
the Romanians the allies decided to play it

00:07:49.009 --> 00:07:55.050
safe and before doing anything asked Kun to
adhere to the same demarcation line that made

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:56.659
Károlyi’s government resign.

00:07:56.659 --> 00:08:02.189
Kun obviously declined and so everyone started
preparing for war, again.

00:08:02.189 --> 00:08:07.189
On the 15th of April, Hungarians launched
an unsuccessful preemptive attack on the Romanians

00:08:07.189 --> 00:08:11.899
who then followed with a counter attack, after
some heavy fighting the Romanians were able

00:08:11.899 --> 00:08:16.449
to break the Hungarian lines and against the
protest of the Allies pushed into Hungary

00:08:16.449 --> 00:08:20.929
all the way to the Tisza river, here the communists
were finally able to hold them.

00:08:20.929 --> 00:08:25.690
During the continuation of the Hungarian Romanian
war, Hungarians were hoping for a large soviet

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:30.650
attack on the Romanian controlled Bessarabia
but considering the Soviets were preoccupied

00:08:30.650 --> 00:08:35.909
fighting the Ukranians, Poles and White Russians,
no major attack came and the smaller ones

00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:38.770
that did come were repelled by the Romanians.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:44.250
On the 20th of May 1919 with the Tisza line
holding the Hungarians started a new offencive

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:49.360
into Slovakia successfully pushing back the
unprepared Czechoslovak forces, the Romanians

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:54.160
tried a counter attack from the east to preserve
a land connection with Czechoslovakia but

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:58.750
this was successfully repelled by the Hungarians
who eventually split the connection between

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:03.420
the two countries while gaining control over
much of South Eastern Slovakia by the 16th

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:04.420
of June.

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:08.970
On that same day Hungarians proclaimed the
formation of the Slovak Soviet Republic which

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.050
was meant to be a communist puppet state of
Hungary.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:16.889
This was done mostly to try to get the support
of Slovak communists and nationalists hoping

00:09:16.889 --> 00:09:18.440
for independent Slovakia.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:23.029
However this backfired tremendously with not
many Slovaks supporting the state and many

00:09:23.029 --> 00:09:28.139
Hungarians dispyising its very existence as
they thought the Hungarian Communists would

00:09:28.139 --> 00:09:33.230
bring all the former lands directly under
Hungarian control, not create communist puppet

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:34.230
states.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:38.870
Due to this the Communist Control over Hungary
started wavering, losing support from most

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:42.160
people other than proletariats in major cities.

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:46.750
Large desertion also started to happen within
the Hungairan army and soon the Slovak Soviet

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:50.769
Republic fell as the Hungarians were pushed
out of Czechoslovakia.

00:09:50.769 --> 00:09:54.720
Also during this time Yugoslavian forces occupied
more of southern Hungary.

00:09:54.720 --> 00:10:00.829
In late July 1919 a last ditch offensive was
conducted by the Hungarians trying to break

00:10:00.829 --> 00:10:02.480
the Romanian Tisza line.

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.449
This proved to be unsuccessful and the Romanians
counterattacked with the goal of reaching

00:10:06.449 --> 00:10:12.040
Budapest which they did the 3rd of August,
ending the Hungarian Soviet Republic.

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:16.579
What followed next was a complicated set of
diplomatic and political negotiations between

00:10:16.579 --> 00:10:21.180
the multiple counter revolutionary rightist
administrations and the allies, all while

00:10:21.180 --> 00:10:26.540
a largely Romanian occupation of most of Hungary
outside of the Balton area took place.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:31.610
The Romanian occupation wasn’t civil and
the Romanians looted pretty much anything

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:37.910
from large mechanical industrial installations
to train engines, cattle, horses, etc. basically

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:41.140
anything that could benefit the post war Romanian
state.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:46.470
It was during this political uncertainty that
a former admiral of the Austro-Hunagrian Navy

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:50.759
Miklós Horthy started to gain a very strong
power base in the Balaton area.

00:10:50.759 --> 00:10:56.209
He helped form and became the military leader
of the new Hunagarian army and onse Romanians

00:10:56.209 --> 00:11:01.339
due to an order from the allies withdrew from
Budapest Horthy along with his army entered

00:11:01.339 --> 00:11:04.819
the city 16th of November 1919.

00:11:04.819 --> 00:11:09.390
Eventually from all this instability and after
a lot of negotiating with the allies a monarchist

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:13.769
government was able to get into power re-establishing
the Kingdom of Hungary.

00:11:13.769 --> 00:11:17.980
The problem was even though the allies were
at this point willing to tolerate the new

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:23.209
monarchist government over the communist one,
they still were firmly against any return

00:11:23.209 --> 00:11:25.610
of a habsburg rule in central Europe.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:30.100
So the monarchist government did the second
best thing they could and elected a universally

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:35.189
liked war hero Horthy who also had control
over the country's military as the regent

00:11:35.189 --> 00:11:38.529
to the Kingdom of Hungary in March of 1920.

00:11:38.529 --> 00:11:42.399
Also during this time reprisal attacks for
the red terror started to be conducted by

00:11:42.399 --> 00:11:47.170
fascists members operating within Horthies’
army and the new monarchist government.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:52.259
These killings became to be known as the white
terror and they reached a far bigger height

00:11:52.259 --> 00:11:55.290
and death toll than the red terror attacks
ever did.

00:11:55.290 --> 00:12:00.560
Targets included former communists, jews and
intellectuals deemed to be too much on the

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:01.560
left.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:05.689
To what extent Horthy was involved or knew
about these killings is a matter of debate

00:12:05.689 --> 00:12:07.930
and far beyond the scope of this video.

00:12:07.930 --> 00:12:12.649
But now finally with a new government in Hungary
that wasn't in an active war with the allies,

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:17.850
the peace negotiations in Paris that dealt
with Hungary could resume.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:22.190
As you would imagine most of the allies were
pretty fed up with Hungary at this point.

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:26.999
Not only did they actively try to go against
the post war terms imposed on them but then

00:12:26.999 --> 00:12:31.630
formed a soviet republic and engaged in another
war against the allies.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:35.769
Therefore the Hungarian delegation didn’t
really have much good will during the drafting

00:12:35.769 --> 00:12:39.670
of the peace treaty and pretty much had to
sign anything the allies gave them.

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:44.949
When it comes to the peace negotiations themselves
the most sighted point today is the use of

00:12:44.949 --> 00:12:46.170
the 1910 ethnic census.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:47.170
From which this map was made.

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:51.130
However just like with the Austrian map this
map doesn’t show ethnic boundaries.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:56.029
The Hungarian 1910 census only asked for a
person's “native language”.

00:12:56.029 --> 00:13:00.610
From this data it was then assumed that one's
native language defines also their ethnicity

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.750
and so an ethnic map was made.

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:07.110
Now asking for someone's “native language”
is still a better strategy to define one's

00:13:07.110 --> 00:13:11.400
ethnicity than asking for a “Umgangssprache”
but it isn’t perfect.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:17.120
For example 65% of German speakers in today's
Slovakia spoke a second language natively

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:21.879
and there were many native bilingual or even
trilingual people in the kingdom.

00:13:21.879 --> 00:13:26.860
Therefore people like let's say natively bilingual
Romanians sometimes reported Hungarian as

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:31.620
their native language since that was the main
language of the kingdom even though they considered

00:13:31.620 --> 00:13:33.949
themself as Romanian not Hungarian.

00:13:33.949 --> 00:13:38.509
However, this discrepancy isn’t huge like
some Romanian or Slovak nationalists would

00:13:38.509 --> 00:13:44.439
have you believe and this map is largely accurate
if we try to use it to define ethnic boundaries,

00:13:44.439 --> 00:13:50.279
even though the map itself shows people’s
self identified native language not ethnicity.

00:13:50.279 --> 00:13:54.879
Another thing to watchout for is that this
map even though very detailed shows just the

00:13:54.879 --> 00:13:57.339
majority native language in an area.

00:13:57.339 --> 00:14:02.149
The fact that a random province in Transilvania
has a majority Romanian speaking population

00:14:02.149 --> 00:14:05.050
doesn’t mean there were no Hungarians.

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:09.779
Therefore this map, which does look weird,
is actually a better representation of the

00:14:09.779 --> 00:14:12.279
native language divisions in the kingdom.

00:14:12.279 --> 00:14:17.290
But such a map is hard to use on a geographical
scale so let's go back to the other one.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:20.180
When looking at this map few things come to
light.

00:14:20.180 --> 00:14:24.889
One is that it’s obviously impossible to
draw borders in such a way that there wouldn’t

00:14:24.889 --> 00:14:27.129
be any people living outside of their country.

00:14:27.129 --> 00:14:32.209
Two if you roughly averaged it out the borders
of new Hungary should look somewhat like this

00:14:32.209 --> 00:14:34.899
if you go by ethnicity as a deciding factor.

00:14:34.899 --> 00:14:38.290
However the borders of Hungary ended up looking
like this.

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:43.959
This was because ethnicity was a factor in
the peace negotiations but not the only factor

00:14:43.959 --> 00:14:45.980
as many people make it out to be.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:51.620
As stated before, Hungary was far from a favorable
place in the negotiations and the allies wanted

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:56.470
to make sure that it would never unify with
Austria or be able to attack its neighboring

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:58.749
nations like it did a year prior.

00:14:58.749 --> 00:15:04.589
This meant that land which had Hungarian majority
but was strategically important like for example

00:15:04.589 --> 00:15:07.339
the Szatmárnémeti (Satu Mare), Nagyvárad
(Oradea), and Arad railway line were given

00:15:07.339 --> 00:15:11.339
to Romania despite having a Hungarian majority
population.

00:15:11.339 --> 00:15:16.139
Same thing with the south Slovak railway line
or even the very valuable control over the

00:15:16.139 --> 00:15:17.279
Danube river.

00:15:17.279 --> 00:15:22.769
Effectively making Hungary weaker while strengthening
the new entente allies in central Europe.

00:15:22.769 --> 00:15:26.440
This statement from the French Prime minister
Clémenceau (klémansó) summarizes the allied

00:15:26.440 --> 00:15:29.290
intent with the treaty of Trianon and Saint
Germain.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:33.749
“Our firmest guarantee against German [and
Soviet] aggression is that behind Germany,

00:15:33.749 --> 00:15:38.939
in an excellent strategic position, stand
Czechoslovakia, Poland [and Romania]”

00:15:38.939 --> 00:15:43.800
So the new allied nations like Czechoslovakia,
Poland, Romania, and Yugoslavia were not only

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:48.639
given very favorable peace deals because they
fought on the allied side but also because

00:15:48.639 --> 00:15:53.189
the allies thought if these new nations were
strong enough they would act as a deterrent

00:15:53.189 --> 00:15:58.029
against German, Austrian, Hunagarian and now
the new enemy Soviet aggression.

00:15:58.029 --> 00:16:02.910
And so the Hungairans were forced to sign
a very unfavorable peace treaty on the 4th

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:05.769
of June in the Grand Trianon Palace in Versailles.

00:16:05.769 --> 00:16:10.149
It would actually take a couple of years and
few revisions before all the particulars of

00:16:10.149 --> 00:16:14.509
the treaty would be in effect but for all
intents and purposes this was the treaty that

00:16:14.509 --> 00:16:18.390
defined with few exceptions the borders of
modern Hungary.

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:22.819
However breaking up a centuries old empire
doesn’t only present an ethnic issue but

00:16:22.819 --> 00:16:24.999
also a giant economic one.

00:16:24.999 --> 00:16:29.809
The Austro-Hungarian Empire was one country
and its industrial infrastructure reflected

00:16:29.809 --> 00:16:30.809
this.

00:16:30.809 --> 00:16:35.339
Due to completely new borders in central europe,
domestic trade became foreign trade, and many

00:16:35.339 --> 00:16:38.240
factories were cut off from their raw materials.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:43.290
For example spinning mills remained in Austria
while weaving mills in Czechoslovakia.

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:47.879
The grain mills in Budapest, at the time one
the largest in Europe, after the break up

00:16:47.879 --> 00:16:52.540
had to operate on only 20% capacity due to
insufficient grain supply.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:57.839
And even then post war Hungary still produced
500% more agricultural goods than it needed

00:16:57.839 --> 00:17:02.070
since its industry was focused on being the
breadbasket of the old Empire.

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:09.039
By 1925 the trade of common goods in central
Europe fell by 54% when compared to 1914 and

00:17:09.039 --> 00:17:12.809
that is with the inclusion of Austro-Hungarian
internal trade of common goods during that

00:17:12.809 --> 00:17:13.809
time.

00:17:13.809 --> 00:17:18.669
The economies of these countries would eventually
recover specially in Czechoslovakia that inherited

00:17:18.669 --> 00:17:24.110
75% of the empire's industrial capacity and
in Austria which had the highest infrastructure

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:28.140
development, standards of living and education
in the former Empire and therefor was able

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:33.710
to by 1929 have the highest GDP per capita
from all the former countries of Austria-Hungary.

00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:38.710
But with all that said, despite the recovery
the setbacks of the division of the empire

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:42.700
were ever present in all the former countries'
economies.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:49.659
In the end, in the age of nationalism Austria-Hungary
tried to run a multicultural empire that refused

00:17:49.659 --> 00:17:53.030
to reform (although not without a lack of
trying), as such its breakup at the first

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:57.760
sign of major instability which came during
the Great War was inevitable.

00:17:57.760 --> 00:18:02.570
What people grumble about to this day is whether
the way the break up happened was fair or

00:18:02.570 --> 00:18:06.230
not, which really depends on who you ask.

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:12.539
But in the end a hundred years later, it doesn’t
matter, because we have the EU now, another

00:18:12.539 --> 00:18:18.360
multicultural country, however, hopefully
this time we can overcome our idiotic triabilistic

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:21.559
tendencies and hold together.

00:18:21.559 --> 00:18:26.450
But on a different topic did you know that
an Austro-Hungarian engineer named Gunther

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:31.980
Burstyn, in 1911 proposed to the Austro-Hungarian
military to build his design of arguably the

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:36.990
first ever tank which he called Motorgeschütz,
literally meaning motor gun.

00:18:36.990 --> 00:18:41.870
However, the Austro-Hungarian military declined
his proposal and so Austria-Hungary wasn’t

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:46.380
the first country to build a modern tank but
that shouldn’t stop you from playing around

00:18:46.380 --> 00:18:48.950
in some tank battles in the World of Tanks
video game.

